      "line_number": 6,
      "line_end": 6,
      "title": "SQL injection in user email search",
      "description": "The index action puts params[:q] straight into the SQL text of the where clause. Any authenticated caller controls that value. An authenticated caller can inject SQL to read columns such as api_token or admin flags. The caller could also change rows in the database. Pass the search term as a bound parameter and escape LIKE wildcards with sanitize_sql_like.",
      "suggested_change": "    users = users.where(\"email LIKE ?\", \"%#{User.sanitize_sql_like(params[:q])}%\") if params[:q].present?",
      "source": "semgrep:ruby.rails.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The index action puts params[:q] straight into the SQL text of the where clause. Any authenticated caller controls that value.",
      "consequence": "An authenticated caller can inject SQL to read columns such as api_token or admin flags. The caller could also change rows in the database.",
      "fix": "Pass the search term as a bound parameter and escape LIKE wildcards with sanitize_sql_like."
    },
